  "scope": "Typed retained initial/established SIP consultation metadata, current Store authority, revision/outcome recording and purpose-bound return control. Controlled Store cases and service compilation only; actual retained/private SIP network profiles remain pending.",
  "implementation": [
    "ConsultationMediaOrigin distinguishes native metadata from an initial or committed SIP origin. The retained remote is selected from its actual media registry; private endpoints remain the existing native pair. SIP metadata never fabricates native peer signing keys or native projections.",
    "A captured SIP snapshot resolves only a previously observed metadata origin in this Store runtime, then checks its entire shape against fresh current call, endpoint, route, membership, credential and lifetime facts. The bounded readiness registry owns metadata alone. Complete authority readers are acquired for the actual planning/attempt; no cached item grants IO.",
    "Current private lifetimes validate retained SIP independently of retired native credentials. Captured audience revisions update the matching initial/established SIP generation rather than a native lifetime. Stored operation identities, original member epochs and same-runtime ownership remain checked.",
    "Return admission includes current selected SIP route authority and original physical binding. Known departure requires recorded exact call/generation/runtime and retired logical state; it grants no media authority. Initial retained readiness recognizes actual accepted answer/connected observations, not an invented native lifetime or a ready row alone.",
    "Purpose-bound SIP return send edges check phone receive permission separately from native receive permission, preserve reciprocal recipient ceilings and exclude private candidates/other private groups. Native/SIP source facts remain separately typed. Held SIP controls preserve parent expiry/cancellation and current source identity and activation before restoring a route.",
    "This increment supports a SIP retained leg with native private endpoints. Selected/private SIP endpoints, remaining DTMF compositions and actual wire verification are still required; no new whole-clause/task/acceptance credit."
  ],
